  m_Name: Activity_Landing
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: MarsOutpost.Runtime::MarsOutpost.Core.ActivityDefinition
  id: landing
  displayName: Landing Site
  tagline: Choose where the crew touches down.
  description: Compare hazard tags on a fictional training map and pick a landing site.
  icon: {fileID: 0}
  hubOrder: 0
  estimatedMinutes: 2
  requiredForMission: 1
  simulationNote: Landing hazard tags and resource changes are game labels. The training map is fictional art - not NASA or Mars Trek data.
  sceneName: 02_LandingSite
  instructionTitle: Pick a landing site
  instructionBody: 'Study the fictional training map. Tap a numbered marker to compare three hazard tags: slope, dust, and distance from the outpost.


    There is no single perfect site. A short drive saves power, a gentle slope protects the crew, and a site with interesting geology can add science progress.


    Pick the trade-off your crew can live with, then confirm one site.'
